{"name":"Red Hook","hex":"#845544","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Red Hook","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A village and town in Dutchess County, New York.","A neighborhood of Brooklyn, New York City."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Red_Hook"}],"entries":[{"title":"Red Hook, Brooklyn","blocks":[{"text":"Red Hook is a neighborhood in western Brooklyn, New York City, United States, within the area once known as South Brooklyn. It is located on a peninsula projecting into the Upper New York Bay and is bounded by the Gowanus Expressway and the Carroll Gardens neighborhood on the northeast, Gowanus Canal on the east, and the Upper New York Bay on the west and south. A prosperous shipping and port area in the early 20th century, the area declined in the latter part of the century. Today, it is home to the Red Hook Houses, the largest housing project in Brooklyn."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/RH_Houses_East_Lorraine_eve_jeh.jpg/330px-RH_Houses_East_Lorraine_eve_jeh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Hook%2C_Brooklyn"},{"title":"Erie Basin dry dock","blocks":[{"text":"Erie Basin dry dock was a graving dock facility located at Erie Basin, in Red Hook, Brooklyn, New York City. There were at least two docks built, although only one remained into the 21st century. The dock contributed to making Red Hook the \"center of the shipping industry in New York\", and was part of Erie Basin's dry and shipping dock infrastructure, the largest in the city. It was the first graving dock in the United States."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/03-4-4_Todd-Erie-25.jpg/330px-03-4-4_Todd-Erie-25.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erie_Basin_dry_dock"},{"title":"Hook","blocks":[{"text":"A hook is a tool consisting of a length of material, typically metal, that contains a portion that is curved/bent back or has a deeply grooved indentation, which serves to grab, latch or in any way attach itself onto another object. The hook's design allows traction forces to be relayed through the curved/indented portion to and from the proximal end of the hook, which is either a straight shaft or a ring for attachment to a thread, rope or chain, providing a reversible attachment between two objects."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/KamAZ-53213_Kranaufbau.jpg/330px-KamAZ-53213_Kranaufbau.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hook"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/RedHook-Factory.jpg/500px-RedHook-Factory.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/RedHook-Factory.jpg/500px-RedHook-Factory.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" Holland-style factory building in Red Hook","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARedHook-Factory.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Red_hook_circa_1875.gif/500px-Red_hook_circa_1875.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Red_hook_circa_1875.gif/500px-Red_hook_circa_1875.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Brooklyn Heights and Red Hook circa 1875","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARed_hook_circa_1875.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Hurricane_Sandy_610_Smith_St_P1040029.jpg/500px-Hurricane_Sandy_610_Smith_St_P1040029.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Hurricane_Sandy_610_Smith_St_P1040029.jpg/1280px-Hurricane_Sandy_610_Smith_St_P1040029.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Hurricane_Sandy_610_Smith_St_P1040029.jpg/500px-Hurricane_Sandy_610_Smith_St_P1040029.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hurricane Sandy effects seen at 610 Smith Street","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHurricane_Sandy_610_Smith_St_P1040029.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Grand_base_ball_match_for_the_championship%2C_between_the_%27Excelsior%27_and_%27Atlantic%27_clubs%2C_of_Brooklyn%2C_at_the_Excelsior_Grounds%2C_South_Brooklyn%2C_on_Thursday%2C_July_19_-_NYIN_1860.jpg/500px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Grand_base_ball_match_for_the_championship%2C_between_the_%27Excelsior%27_and_%27Atlantic%27_clubs%2C_of_Brooklyn%2C_at_the_Excelsior_Grounds%2C_South_Brooklyn%2C_on_Thursday%2C_July_19_-_NYIN_1860.jpg/1280px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_sour